From: Mark Chiou <chiouss@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: at803x: set IPQ5018 PHY LEDs active high

The IPQ5018 internal PHY is reset in probe, which drops the LED
polarity configured by the bootloader. The PHY then comes up with
active low LEDs and boards wired for active high LEDs, like the
Zyxel NWA220AX-6E, have their port LEDs lit without a link.

Set the LED polarity to active high in config_init, like QSDK does and
like the QCA808x driver does by default for its LEDs.

Signed-off-by: Mark Chiou <chiouss@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/qcom/at803x.c	2026-09-29 15:57:30.312122995 +0800
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/qcom/at803x.c	2026-09-29 15:57:30.340926517 +0800
@@ -151,6 +151,10 @@
 #define IPQ5018_PHY_DEBUG_ANA_LDO_EFUSE_DEFAULT	0x50
 #define IPQ5018_PHY_DEBUG_ANA_DAC_FILTER	0xa080
 
+#define IPQ5018_PHY_MMD7_LED_POLARITY_CTRL	0x901a
+/* QSDK sets 0x46 to this register, BIT 6 makes the LEDs active high */
+#define IPQ5018_PHY_LED_ACTIVE_HIGH		BIT(6)
+
 MODULE_DESCRIPTION("Qualcomm Atheros AR803x PHY driver");
 MODULE_AUTHOR("Matus Ujhelyi");
 MODULE_LICENSE("GPL");
@@ -1037,6 +1041,18 @@
 {
 	struct ipq5018_priv *priv = phydev->priv;
 	u16 val;
+	int ret;
+
+	/*
+	 * The PHY is reset in probe, which drops the LED polarity set up by
+	 * the bootloader. Default to active high LEDs like QSDK does and the
+	 * QCA808x driver does for its LEDs.
+	 */
+	ret = phy_set_bits_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_AN,
+			       IPQ5018_PHY_MMD7_LED_POLARITY_CTRL,
+			       IPQ5018_PHY_LED_ACTIVE_HIGH);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
 
 	/*
 	 * set LDO efuse: first temporarily store ANA_DAC_FILTER value from
